      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256025/assets/2090e695566d64097143c31d83e17ea965cd899a2ed3e91536242f84bf538961.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $x$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{5}{2}$ to give $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5}).$\n\n- Finally, shift it **up** by $3$ units to give $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+3.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+3.$",
